@startuml class
left to right direction
class User {
  +id: Integer
  +name: String
  +email: String
  +password_hash: String
  +role: String
  +set_password(password)
  +check_password(password): Boolean
}

class FoodListing {
  +id: Integer
  +vendor_id: Integer
  +title: String
  +description: Text
  +portions: Integer
  +pickup_location: String
  +dietary_tags: String
  +pickup_start: DateTime
  +pickup_end: DateTime

}

class DietaryTag{
   +id: Integer
   +name: String
}

class Reservation{
  +id: Integer
  +listing_id: Integer
  +student_id: Integer
  +portions: Integer
  +pickup_code: String
  +status: String
  +created_at: DateTime
}

User "1" -- "0..*" FoodListing : creates (vendor)
User "1" -- "0..*" Reservation : places (student)
FoodListing "1" -- "0..*" Reservation : receives
FoodListing "0..*" .. "0..*" DietaryTag : tagged with (planned)

note right of User
  US1: role = student or vendor.
  creation_date / active not verified.
end note

note bottom of FoodListing
  US2 implementation currently stores
  dietary_tags as a String.
  DietaryTag association is a proposed
  normalized design, not yet implemented.
end note

note bottom of Reservation
  US4 planned model; verify against
  implementation when US4 is developed.
end note


@enduml